{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC8SuperExpBound"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel.aDClassical_coeff_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel.aDClassical_coeff_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingClassicalKernel.lean#L81-L88","doc":"The classical kernel is **not** the fixed-`τ` model: at a place where the variable\ncoefficient `(n+2)` differs from the constant one, the two recurrences disagree. Concretely\nthe leading multiplier is `(n+2)`, which is unbounded — no constant `τ` matches it for all\n`n`. (The quantitative failure beyond the seed is `Lever1Depth2Exclusion`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel.aDClassical_variable_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel.aDClassical_variable_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingClassicalKernel.lean#L59-L79","doc":"**The exact classical binding kernel is variable-coefficient (derived, not fitted).**\n\nFor every `n`, the classical binding period `a_D^(n) = I(n)/n` satisfies the\nvariable-coefficient depth-2 recurrence\n\n  `(n+3)·a_D^(n+3) = (n+2)·a_D^(n+2) + (n+2)(n+1)·a_D^(n+1)`.\n\nThe coefficients depend on `n` (they grow), so this is **not** a fixed-`τ` recurrence; the\nconstant-`τ` depth-2 model (`BindingRecurrenceSpectral`) is the n≤4 shadow of this kernel.\nProved from the telephone recurrence — no fit, no `sorry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel.involutionNumber_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel.involutionNumber_shift","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingClassicalKernel.lean#L54-L57","doc":"The telephone recurrence, in the shape needed below (definitional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel.aDClassical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingClassicalKernel.aDClassical","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingClassicalKernel.lean#L50-L52","doc":"Classical-limit (`q = 1`) binding period `a_D^(n) = I(n)/n`, `I =` involution numbers\n(`= (Σ_{λ⊢n} f^λ)/n` via Identity I). ","signatureChunk":0}]}